questions.questionText:
Wavefunctions and energies for a particle confined in a cubic box are 𝜓𝑛_{𝑥},𝑛_{𝑦},𝑛_{𝑧} and 𝐸_{𝑛𝑥,𝑛𝑦,𝑛𝑧}, respectively. The functions 𝜙_{1}, 𝜙_{2}, 𝜙_{3}, and 𝜙_{4} are written as linear combinations of 𝜓_{𝑛𝑥,𝑛𝑦,𝑛𝑧}. Among these functions, the eigenfunction(s) of the Hamiltonian operator for this particle is/are

𝜙_{1} = \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}\}) 𝜓_{1,4,1} -1 \sqrt{2} 𝜓_{2,2,3}

𝜙_{2} = \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}\}) 𝜓_{1,5,1} + \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}\}) 𝜓_{3,3,3}

𝜙_{3} = \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}\}) 𝜓_{1,3,8} + \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}\}) 𝜓_{3,8,1}

𝜙_{4} = \(\frac{1}{2}\) 𝜓_{3,3,1} + \(\frac{\sqrt{3}{2}\}) 𝜓_{2,4,1}

